{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1464817-a-wyrm-tainted-funeral-company-and-it-s-ceo","id":1464817,"title":"A Wyrm Tainted Funeral Company and it's CEO","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-21T19:59:27-07:00","id":1464817,"title":"A Wyrm Tainted Funeral Company and it's CEO","content":"Hey everyone, this is my first time on this forum in over a year and during this time I joined a play by post group for Werewolf on Discord. Sooner or later I am planning on running a couple of storylines for this group, one of them involves a Wyrm tainted Funeral Company, Capelli Funerals, and it's eccentric CEO, Rodolpho Capelli.<br /> <br /> My idea for Capelli Funerals is that while it's not a PENTEX subsidiary, it has tight connections to it via Magadon, who uses it for funerals and burials for both their employees and recommends them to the grieving families of dead patients. Capelli sells itself as a benevolent company that guides it's clients through both the funeral and grieving process and provides dead loved ones with a comfortable and dignified farewell, which seems to be true on the outside. However, the company is rotten to the core, and knowing servants to the Wyrm. They became a national brand as part of a final &quot; investment project&quot; by either James Kiker or Elliot Meiche before they perished for purposes still unknown to the rest of the Board.<br /> <br /> Capelli secretly uses the bodies in their care for spreading the Wyrn's corrupting influence. They sell bodies to various interested parties from the mob, whom they still have tight connections too, PENTEX, all the way to BSD's who use the dead cadavers for horrific rituals, or for food. They also leave their cemeteries poorly guarded and secretly encourage both grave defilement and grave robbery, and charge the deceased's family high sums for clean-up or for &quot;grave insurance. This is only the tip of the iceberg for Capelli's sins, which feed the Wyrm and ruins Gaia even more.<br /> <br /> Rodolpho Capelli.himself is the grandson of Salvatore Capelli, an Italian immigrant who founded the company in the 20s to serve the Italian-American population. Rodolpho himself is a dumpy, apple-cheeked man in his late 50s, early 60s with white hair, blue eyes, and a winning smile. Often described as the &quot;Mr. Rodgers&quot; of the Funeral industry, Capelli is known as a friendly and gregarious man who is able to get anyone to trust him, his friendly voice and grandfatherly demeanor putting even the most well-guarded people at ease.<br /> <br /> However, this is only a ruse, Capelli is actually a servant of the Wyrm, something that began in the 70s when he took over Capelli from his dead Father, and immediately became an associate for a powerful mob family, one day wanting to be made. He used the cadavers he cared for to smuggle drugs across the state he lived in, used his crematoriums to dispose of any evidence the mob wanted him to, and worse of all, did a few contract killing, his favorite being the one where he buried a man alive. He eventually became a servant of the Wyrm, and met Kiker or Meiche, who wanted to spread his company across the USA, which Capelli was eager to have happen. <br /> <br /> After Kiker or Meiche died, Capelli did not take it well and started becoming unhinged. He regarded Kiker or Meiche as his best friend and grew more and more obsessed with him as the years went on, eventually managing to creep out the Board Member to the point he was planning on having Capelli killed, but was killed before he could by whatever fate awaited them. My idea is that Adrain Newberyy, after decapitating their corpse, gave Kiker's or Meiche's headless body to Capelli, who now keeps it as the centerpiece of a disturbing shrine to his &quot;fallen friend&quot;, with a second shrine awaiting Andre Baptiste, who is helping Capelli boost up his image before a public buyout by Magadon.<br /> <br /> I wish to have advice on other illcit activiestes Capelli Funerals could be up to in service to the Wyrm. I also wish to have advice on making Rodolpho himself an interesting antagonist and how to make his obsession with Meiche or Kiker disturbing, but not to disturbing and how to make it a interesting part of the arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T05:59:17-07:00","id":1464862,"title":"","content":"On the matter of Kiker or Meiche as dead patron-friend, i have <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OawrlVoQqSs\" target=\"_blank\">a simple opinion/answer</a>, if you don't mind, one that kind of justifies Capelli's increasingly uhinged state to boot.... <br /> <br /> Also, might he or someone else in his business be connected to wraiths or spectres, or are his dirty enterprises of a mostly mundane focus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:01:05-07:00","id":1464951,"title":"","content":"Looks fun.<br /> <br /> You may find <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1173822-pentex-research-inspiration-company-by-company?p=1227893#post1227893\">this post from a couple of years ago</a> useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:27:15-07:00","id":1464954,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tip No. Clicked the link and it provided me some interesting ideas to spice up Capelli's company, especially the bits about organ harvesting, which I can see Rodolpho and his mob associates getting into, not to mention the Banes and other unsavory bits that can be laced into the organs..<br /> <br /> Not sure about any connections to Spectres yet, but him having Kiker and Meiche as friends/displays makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> I am now wondering how much taint the shrines of Kiker and Meiche would carry, especially since they are displaying their dead bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}